  <!-- © 2026 melo-foundation -->

  <name>melo</name>
  <summary>YouTube integrated native desktop music player</summary>

  <description>
    <p>
      melo plays music from YouTube. Search, queue, and start a radio from any
      track; build a library and download tracks for offline play; import audio
      files from disk and tag them automatically.
    </p>
    <p>
      It crossfades, skips silent intros and outros, and plays gapless when the
      crossfade is off. There is a ten-band equaliser, a projectM visualiser,
      timed lyrics where they exist, a mini player, and themes you can split
      into colours, style, size and background and share separately.
    </p>
    <p>
      Plugins run out of process and declare what they need; every permission is
      granted by you, per plugin.
    </p>
  </description>

  <launchable type="desktop-id">melo.desktop</launchable>

  <!-- The GitHub handle only. Deliberately no address: the maintainer's
       inbox is not part of the public record. -->
